00:13:12.622 --> 00:13:16.360
Yeah. Think about the thing about quality&nbsp;
control is that it's such an integral part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:22.600
of just product quality. So it's important&nbsp;
to realize that for the exact same product,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:26.600
even if they use the exact same tooling,&nbsp;
the same process, the same materials,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:30.840
if you don't have quality control at all, in&nbsp;
the extreme, that's where you're going to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:36.760
quality issues. Every single production line&nbsp;
is going to have some rate of quality issues.

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:42.520
And the really great factories, the ones that&nbsp;
have very strict quality control guidelines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:46.600
and they're very careful about things, they're&nbsp;
the ones where the final product at a much higher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:51.840
rate is going to provide you with the kind&nbsp;
of quality that you're actually looking for.

