I think for us, whenever we work with factories,&nbsp;
it's all about setting the right expectations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:31.120
You do have to have a bit of flexibility&nbsp;
working within their framework. But during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:37.960
that due diligence process for us, we're striving&nbsp;
to find factories that have top-notch QC systems.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:44.320
That way, we just know whenever we're asking.&nbsp;
For example, if we're scaling up a DTC brand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:51.120
that's going from 20,000 to 100,000 units, in&nbsp;
those situations, we need production schedules.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:55.280
Anyone that we work with in&nbsp;
general, on the factory side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.280 --> 00:15:00.600
they give us that information before we even start&nbsp;
the scale, like, the client starts the scaling.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:05.840
So. it's just important to make sure you're&nbsp;
working with quality people, and then you can kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

